Title: 0003-makerules-aros-no-host-libcrypto
Repository: mupdf
Base-Commit: ce933bdebe05fe54ba9d69792ed268efd9e00047
Requires: 0002-pdf-parse-timegm-for-aros.patch
Author: aros-foliopdf project
Date: 2026-11-08
Upstream-Status: local-only
Scope: Makerules, OS=AROS only. The Folio executable does not link libmupdf-pkcs7 and is unchanged by this.

Problem:
  Makerules computes LIBCRYPTO_CFLAGS and LIBCRYPTO_LIBS from the build host's pkg-config before the OS=AROS block resets HAVE_LIBCRYPTO. On a host with an OpenSSL pkg-config file, source/helpers/pkcs7/pkcs7-openssl.c was compiled with -DHAVE_LIBCRYPTO against the host's headers and mutool failed to link against the host's libcrypto.
Solution:
  Clear LIBCRYPTO_CFLAGS and LIBCRYPTO_LIBS in the OS=AROS block next to HAVE_LIBCRYPTO=no.
Validation:
  not-run
Removal:
  Fill in when this is a workaround; permanent fixes say so here.

diff --git a/Makerules b/Makerules
index 42939dded..ec864129d 100644
--- a/Makerules
+++ b/Makerules
@@ -369,6 +369,10 @@ ifeq "$(OS)" "AROS"
   HAVE_X11=no
   HAVE_OBJCOPY=no
   HAVE_LIBCRYPTO=no
+  # Set from the host's pkg-config above; without clearing them the
+  # pkcs7 helper is built against the host's OpenSSL.
+  LIBCRYPTO_CFLAGS :=
+  LIBCRYPTO_LIBS :=
   HAVE_SYS_CURL=no
   HAVE_SYS_LEPTONICA=no
   HAVE_SYS_TESSERACT=no
